@startuml
title After each fix, look again for the limit

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 10
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam ArrowColor #4B5563
skinparam ArrowFontColor #374151
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #4B5563
  FontColor #111827
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}

rectangle "First hypothesis\nRemove the (N, V) logits matrix\nto train longer contexts" as logits #DBEAFE
rectangle "Attention is the credible shared bottleneck\nMLX ran attention unfused in training;\nits backward materializes the full score matrix" as attn #FECACA
rectangle "First fix\nTiled FlashAttention forward and backward\nSaved attention state scales with N x D" as flash #DCFCE7
rectangle "The limit moves to the launch guard\nThe guard budgets a whole launch chain;\nMLX commits large ranges in separate buffers" as guard #FECACA
rectangle "Second fix\nBudget each command buffer\nKeep the safety margin unchanged" as perbuf #DCFCE7
rectangle "Upstream moves it again\nA later MLX release adds a blocked backward\nfor calls without an array mask" as upstream #FEF3C7
rectangle "After every move\nLook again at what now sets the limit" as next #EDE9FE

logits -down-> attn : no demonstrated context gain
attn -down-> flash : remove the quadratic term
flash -right-> guard : exposes a new limit
guard -down-> perbuf : correct the model
perbuf -down-> upstream : the framework changes too
upstream -down-> next

caption Conceptual sequence. It holds no measured values and is not an allocation-lifetime trace.
@enduml
